WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.410 --> 00:00:04.660
Look, not every movie is going to have you
on the edge of your seat.

00:00:04.660 --> 00:00:06.410
After all, they can't all be Con Air.

00:00:06.410 --> 00:00:10.110
"Put the bunny back in the box."

00:00:10.110 --> 00:00:14.941
Still, you'd think that if anyone's going
to stay awake through a whole movie, it's

00:00:14.941 --> 00:00:16.990
the actors who star in them.

00:00:16.990 --> 00:00:19.510
But that's not always how it plays out.

00:00:19.510 --> 00:00:24.660
Whether out of boredom or sheer exhaustion,
here are a few movie stars who've copped to

00:00:24.660 --> 00:00:27.800
dozing off during their own movies.

00:00:27.800 --> 00:00:28.800
Michael Shannon

00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:33.870
There are few actors working today who are
as outspoken as Michael Shannon.

00:00:33.870 --> 00:00:39.190
Whether he's going on a political rant or
trash-talking the entire movie industry, Shannon

00:00:39.190 --> 00:00:41.831
doesn't hesitate to say exactly how he feels.

00:00:41.831 --> 00:00:47.350
In the role of Zod, Shannon had one of the
most crucial parts in Batman v. Superman:

00:00:47.350 --> 00:00:48.720
Dawn of Justice.

00:00:48.720 --> 00:00:52.969
And that's saying a lot, since his character
was pretty much dead part of the time.

00:00:52.969 --> 00:00:57.310
But don't ask Shannon how the rest of the
film turned out, because he slept through

00:00:57.310 --> 00:00:58.310
the thing.

00:00:58.310 --> 00:01:02.399
Shannon told Fandango that the first time
he tried to watch the film, he got punched

00:01:02.399 --> 00:01:08.000
by the Sandman: "I watched it once and I fell
asleep ... I was on an international flight

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:09.970
and I was tired."

00:01:09.970 --> 00:01:10.970
Johnny Depp

00:01:10.970 --> 00:01:16.560
In 2015, Depp earned plenty of praise for
his performance as legendary Boston crime

00:01:16.560 --> 00:01:19.550
boss Whitey Bulger in Black Mass.

00:01:19.550 --> 00:01:24.150
The drama went on to gross a respectable $62
million at the box office, which occurred

00:01:24.150 --> 00:01:29.150
shortly after its high-profile screening at
the Venice International Film Festival.

00:01:29.150 --> 00:01:33.750
Depp was in attendance for that — or at
least his physical form was.

00:01:33.750 --> 00:01:38.020
He later confessed on Jimmy Kimmel Live that
he didn't make it all the way through the

00:01:38.020 --> 00:01:39.020
movie.

00:01:39.020 --> 00:01:40.020
"And fell asleep in the movie?

00:01:40.020 --> 00:01:42.730
I fell asleep about 15 times.

00:01:42.730 --> 00:01:45.060
I remember my wife was kinda..

00:01:45.060 --> 00:01:45.880
Empf!

00:01:45.880 --> 00:01:46.880
Empf!"

00:01:47.760 --> 00:01:49.500
It's not that he didn't like the movie.

00:01:49.500 --> 00:01:55.490
It's just that, as he explained, he has, quote,
"a problem watching films of any kind, unless

00:01:55.490 --> 00:01:57.160
it's a documentary."

00:01:57.160 --> 00:02:01.650
One of the highest-paid actors alive hates
watching movies.

00:02:01.650 --> 00:02:02.650
Huh.

00:02:02.650 --> 00:02:04.020
Brenton Thwaites

00:02:04.020 --> 00:02:09.720
Jeff Bridges tried to bring Lois Lowry's young
adult dystopian classic The Giver to the big

00:02:09.720 --> 00:02:12.220
screen for more than two decades.

00:02:12.220 --> 00:02:17.061
And when he began the process in the mid-nineties,
he envisioned his father, Lloyd Bridges, in

00:02:17.061 --> 00:02:18.170
the title role.

00:02:18.170 --> 00:02:23.880
By the time the movie came out in 2014, though,
Jeff Bridges himself was old enough to play

00:02:23.880 --> 00:02:24.880
the Giver.

00:02:24.880 --> 00:02:29.460
The role of Jonas, the Young Person Who Will
Save the World, went to Australian actor Brenton

00:02:29.460 --> 00:02:30.460
Thwaites.

00:02:30.460 --> 00:02:35.450
Despite the career-making potential of the
part, Thwaites actually dozed off the first

00:02:35.450 --> 00:02:36.870
time he watched The Giver.

00:02:36.870 --> 00:02:41.070
He told Nova 106.9: "They set up a screening
with me and Jeff [Bridges].

00:02:41.070 --> 00:02:44.230
I was so tired that I kept falling asleep,
during my own movie."

00:02:44.230 --> 00:02:47.000
Shia LaBeouf

00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:51.670
Performance art stunts have kind of become
Shia LaBeouf's thing in recent years.

00:02:51.670 --> 00:02:56.990
Not too long ago, he decided to live alone
in a cabin in Finland for a month, just because

00:02:56.990 --> 00:02:58.500
he's Shia LaBeouf.

00:02:58.500 --> 00:02:59.800
"Living in the woods.

00:02:59.800 --> 00:03:00.820
Shia Lebeouf."

00:03:01.120 --> 00:03:02.440
"Living for sport.

00:03:02.440 --> 00:03:03.440
Shia Lebeouf."

00:03:03.640 --> 00:03:05.680
"Eating all the bodies."

00:03:06.100 --> 00:03:08.120
"Actual cannibal, Shia Lebeouf."

00:03:08.120 --> 00:03:14.370
So back in December 2015, Shia LaBeouf famously
held a film festival in his own honor at the

00:03:14.370 --> 00:03:17.210
Angelika Film Center in New York.

00:03:17.210 --> 00:03:22.420
Titled, conveniently, #ALLMYMOVIES, the film
festival involved LaBeouf sitting in a movie

00:03:22.420 --> 00:03:27.720
theater and watching every movie he's ever
starred in, in reverse chronological order.

00:03:27.720 --> 00:03:32.010
That's about three day's worth of films, so
it's understandable that LaBeouf fell asleep

00:03:32.010 --> 00:03:33.010
at some point.

00:03:33.010 --> 00:03:37.900
When he did finally doze off, it was to Transformers:
Dark of the Moon.

00:03:37.900 --> 00:03:39.040
And he wasn't alone.

00:03:39.040 --> 00:03:41.170
Describing the event, he later said:

00:03:41.170 --> 00:03:44.640
"[During] Transformers 2 they could feel when
I sunk in my seat.

00:03:44.640 --> 00:03:46.540
That’s not a performative thing.

00:03:46.540 --> 00:03:49.650
That’s me going through some kind of crisis.

00:03:49.650 --> 00:03:50.790
And I’m not the only one.

00:03:50.790 --> 00:03:56.090
I remember right before I fell asleep I looked
next to me and the guy next to me was falling

00:03:56.090 --> 00:03:57.090
asleep.

00:03:57.090 --> 00:03:59.260
You can see it on the screenshot we’re both
asleep.

00:03:59.260 --> 00:04:01.200
And the guy behind us is asleep."

00:04:09.300 --> 00:04:10.300
Thanks for watching!

